MidnightBSD names itself in os.name, so bazel falls through to OS.UNKNOWN and
then picks the Linux sources and constraints: the build stops in
unix_jni_linux.cc for want of sys/xattr.h (run 35736537908).  It is a FreeBSD
derivative -- the kernel runs FreeBSD binaries, the compiler defines
__FreeBSD__, and mports ships the FreeBSD openjdk -- so answer FreeBSD.
CI only.

--- a/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/util/OS.java	2026-09-22 23:33:01
+++ b/src/main/java/com/google/devtools/build/lib/util/OS.java	2026-09-22 23:33:01
@@ -72,6 +72,14 @@
       return OS.UNKNOWN;
     }
 
+    // MidnightBSD is a FreeBSD derivative: its kernel runs FreeBSD binaries,
+    // its compiler defines __FreeBSD__, and its openjdk is the FreeBSD build.
+    // Everything keyed on the OS wants the FreeBSD answer, and the name is the
+    // only thing that differs.
+    if (osName.startsWith("MidnightBSD")) {
+      return OS.FREEBSD;
+    }
+
     for (OS os : OS.values()) {
       // Windows have many names, all starting with "Windows".
       if (osName.startsWith(os.detectionName)) {
